version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KrasForge/unk-deaddrop-companion"
abstract: "Defensive research companion for the UNK_DeadDrop artifact study. Includes a parse-only JavaScript AST scanner, inert boundary fixtures, and 33 experimental YARA file-content rules in 28 files. Scanner 0.2.0 is published on npm and PyPI; this archive contains newer scanner source changes that have not yet been released to those registries. Every YARA rule matched retained case artifacts in a read-only replay; a small local software baseline produced no hits. Authentic endpoint logs were unavailable, so Sigma event rules are not included. The available corpus does not establish production precision or recall, execution, collection, attribution, or current infrastructure status."
keywords:
  - malware analysis
  - detection engineering
  - static analysis
  - YARA
